Consecutive module declarations without a body (`mod cli;`) print on one outline line with their names, its line range spanning them, as a `lib.rs` declaring dozens of modules reads best.
- Only modules declared alike join: the same visibility, no leading annotations, and each on the line right after the previous one. A blank line, a `#[cfg(test)]` or doc comment, another visibility, or an inline `mod name { … }` starts a new line.
- `use` declarations aren't joined: a `pub use` prints its whole path, which joined lines would make too long to read.
== args
input/lib.rs
== file input/lib.rs
//! Library.

mod cli;
mod discovery;
mod outline;

pub mod engines;
pub mod sources;
/// Test helpers.
pub mod testing;
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests;
mod inline {}
pub use outline::Outline;
pub use sources::Source;
== stdout
input/lib.rs (15 lines)
Library.
[L3-L5] mod cli, discovery, outline
[L7-L8] pub mod engines, sources
[L9-L10] pub mod testing
[L11-L12] mod tests
[L13-L13] mod inline
[L14-L14] pub use outline::Outline
[L15-L15] pub use sources::Source
